                        "sense_id": "cbc6f2ed-1ba8-39ae-a2e0-48f3748c0f6b",
                        "entry_id": "58530529-2c27-3aac-aa51-3eca6021a0ef",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Advocating or practising feudalism, or in which feudalism is practised."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "04b160af-9ce3-446f-9e18-8a158974e34e",
                                "sense_id": "cbc6f2ed-1ba8-39ae-a2e0-48f3748c0f6b",
                                "text": "The sole object of Caesar was, while making use of the existing dynastic, feudalist, and hegemonic divisions, to arrange matters in the interest of Rome, and to bring everywhere into power the men favourably disposed to the foreign rule."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b2bbd508-a3dd-4209-a52a-9b945f7ec293",
                                "sense_id": "cbc6f2ed-1ba8-39ae-a2e0-48f3748c0f6b",
                                "text": "The Chinese gentry, so far as they still existed, preferred to work with him rather than with the feudalist Huns."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "64a57642-5307-412d-a602-f7c8046eb26e",
                                "sense_id": "cbc6f2ed-1ba8-39ae-a2e0-48f3748c0f6b",
                                "text": "Had I been born in a feudalist society, I would have attempted to batter myself into the nobility."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "2abb51de-228e-3ae1-aeee-2e7976f520fd",
                "word": "feudalist",
