                        "form": "feudalists"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9475b05e-34b7-3e0f-8d82-616b3445d848",
                        "entry_id": "2abb51de-228e-3ae1-aeee-2e7976f520fd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An advocate or practitioner of feudalism."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "43c7d92f-9fb1-4079-96bb-feadbc0fdedb",
                                "sense_id": "9475b05e-34b7-3e0f-8d82-616b3445d848",
                                "text": "The author is not a monarchist, an aristocrat, a democrat, a feudalist, nor an advocate of what are called mixed governments like the English, at least for his own country; but is simply an American, devoted to the real, living, and energizing constitution of the American republic as it is, not as some may fancy it might be, or are striving to make it."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e3dbb88d-7c04-4341-8784-e34d0e104240",
                                "sense_id": "9475b05e-34b7-3e0f-8d82-616b3445d848",
                                "text": "His revolt is not a revolt of the commercialist against the feudalist, of the Nonconformist against the Churchman, of the Free-trader against the Protectionist, of the Liberal against the Tory."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "56153e4a-0043-40e3-a766-9af2e35cdc6c",
                                "sense_id": "9475b05e-34b7-3e0f-8d82-616b3445d848",
                                "text": "On this point there was no difference between mercantilists and feudalists, between crowned planners and vested interests, between centralizing bureaucrats and conservative particularists."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2ed880dc-2e8c-4369-9eb5-900117a49619",
                                "sense_id": "9475b05e-34b7-3e0f-8d82-616b3445d848",
                                "text": "In short, Jose Antonio, son of a benevolent Spanish dictator who'd been forced out by republicans, was a sentimental feudalist who suspected capitalism and believed in the dole."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
